BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventpages26pastries23380-20260426@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20260927T150537Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260426
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Pages & Pastries
DESCRIPTION:A Civilized Literary Excursion (with Cake) Are you ready to explore Downtown Frederick\, Maryland in impeccable style and mild confusion? Your Clippie will escort you on a scenic two-hour Frederick sightseeing tour\, pointing out local landmarks\, fascinating facts\, and the occasional squirrel with suspicious intent. You’ll laugh\, you’ll learn\, endure discounts and you’ll probably wonder how we got permission for this. First stop: The Curious Iguana\, Downtown Frederick’s beloved independent bookstore\, home to bestsellers\, local authors\, and at least one employee who definitely reads too much. Browse to your heart’s content\, discover hidden literary gems\, or simply pretend you’ve wandered into a BBC period drama about literacy. Then it’s onward to Twin Bears Bakery\, where the air smells of happiness\, butter\, and light moral compromise. There you’ll enjoy handcrafted pastries so good you may consider writing poetry about them (haikus are acceptable). This stop is a highlight among Frederick’s bakery tours\, and you’ll quickly understand why it’s a local favourite. Whether you’re a bibliophile\, a foodie\, or simply looking for unique things to do in Frederick\, Maryland\, Pages & Pastries is the perfect combination of books\, bakeries\, and double-decker bus charm. It’s a Frederick city tour for the curious\, the hungry\, and the happily confused\, mixing stories\, sweets\, and scenic streets into one gloriously crumb-covered adventure. Come hungry. Leave well-read.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pages-%26-pastries/23380/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfrederickinthecivilwar23395-20260502@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20260927T150537Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260502
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Frederick in the Civil War
DESCRIPTION:History\, Heroics\, and the Occasional Amputation (Strictly Metaphorical) Right\, gather round\, you historically curious lot! Step smartly aboard as we begin our highly educational meander from the National Museum of Civil War Medicine in Downtown Frederick\, Maryland\, where you’ll learn how doctors once treated nearly everything with brandy\, saws\, and an unwavering sense of optimism. Your guide\, a certified docent and part-time time traveler\, will regale you with tales of battlefield brilliance\, questionable hygiene\, and the astonishing resilience of people who really ought to have taken the day off. So join us for a Frederick Civil War history tour because this isn’t just history… it’s history on the double\, with a head wound and a bandage made from curtains. Perfect for history buffs\, museum lovers\, and anyone searching for unique things to do in Frederick\, Maryland\, this unforgettable Civil War bus tour offers a delightfully British take on America’s most dramatic century.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-in-the-civil-war/23395/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhistoryonthedouble23691-20260523@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20260927T150537Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260523
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:History on the Double
DESCRIPTION:Two decks\, one timeline\, and absolutely no sense of direction. Good morning\, historians\, adventurers\, and anyone who got on the wrong bus but is too polite to admit it! Prepare yourself for an extraordinary expedition aboard our towering yellow vintage London double-decker bus\, now thundering proudly through the streets of Downtown Frederick\, Maryland. You’ll start your day along the scenic Carroll Creek Park\, where our gleaming double-decker waits like a massive custard-colored teapot on wheels. Once aboard\, take your seat\, clutch your belongings\, and abandon all responsibility\, our Clippies will handle the chaos from here. As we trundle through historic Downtown Frederick\, you’ll be treated to a fully guided Frederick history tour through centuries of local stories\, from colonial shenanigans to architectural brilliance\, from Civil War-era landmarks to the occasional ghost who refuses to pay rent. Perfect for families\, visitors\, history lovers\, and anyone looking for fun things to do in Frederick Maryland\, this unforgettable historical sightseeing tour is your front-row seat to the city’s remarkable past\, served with a generous helping of British wit.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/history-on-the-double/23691/
END:VEVENT
